#: A metronome — any condition, played as a note.
#:
#: `gateOn` turns a `Sig Bool` into a `Sig Gate`: rising edge presses,
#: falling edge releases.  So anything is a note source — a comparison on
#: a ramp, a threshold over an LFO, a threshold over a follower.  Where
#: the release is, is visible in the condition you wrote.

beat : Sig Gate
beat = gateOn (!(x => x < 0.5) (phase 2.0))

env : Sig Float
env = perc 6.0 beat
